# Frontend and UX

- Use functional React components and TypeScript.
- Follow existing App Router and component patterns.
- Prefer server components unless interactivity requires a client component.
- Keep client boundaries small.
- Preserve responsive behavior.
- Provide loading, success, empty, error, and retry states.
- Use one visually dominant primary action per view.
- Explain unfamiliar terms inline.
- Do not expose internal provider names, IDs, or technical errors to end users.
- Use accessible labels, keyboard support, focus states, and adequate contrast.
- Avoid dense layouts and excessive cards.
- Use existing design tokens and shared components before adding new styling systems.
- Customer-facing copy should be confident, friendly, and direct.
